From b569398a3e7fc3422fafe56563a18f6b06bcaf02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 22:14:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0233: Onboarding pacing -- shortened first-run tour,
 event-driven nudges take over

Automatic first-run tour shortened from all 13 tabs to just
Dashboard/Heroes/Quests. Manual 'Tour' button replay untouched, still
shows the full walkthrough on demand.

Heroes/Quests get tailored first-run copy via a new optional
description field on OnboardingTour's Step type, kept separate from
the shared STEP_DESCRIPTIONS map so a manual replay later doesn't show
stale 'you start with one hero already' text.

Three new GuidanceManager topics, same existing pattern:
first_hero_recruited (heroes.length >= 2, deliberately not >= 1 since
a fresh guild already starts with one), second_hero_affordable
(gold >= cheapest recruit cost, read from RECRUIT_COST not hardcoded),
guild_hall_intro (same trigger, different target tab -- split into two
topics since GuidanceTopic has a single targetTab).

Toast.tsx: guidance-tier messages (banner: true) now linger ~6.5s
instead of the routine 3.2s, reusing the existing banner signal rather
than adding a new parameter.

Fixed buyChainReplayTier's toast: was targeting 'chains' with
banner: true even though the only way to click that purchase is from
inside Replay Memories itself -- now a plain toast, no redundant
'Go to Discovered Quests' prompt for a tab already open.

No changes to save data or any existing guidance topic's trigger.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npx vite build both pass clean against
the properly re-based tree. Confirmed by script: 17 guidance topics,
zero duplicate ids, recruit-cost minimum resolves to exactly 150
against the live recruit-costs.json.
